":[{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Feynman, Richard Phillips.","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Leighton, Ralph"},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Hutchings, Edward"}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"biography"},{"@authority":"2","#text":"Autobiography"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Autobiographies"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Humor"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Autobiographies"},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Autobiographies."}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}}],"publisher":"W.W. Norton","dateIssued":["1997, c1985",{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"1997"}],"edition":"1st pbk. ed.","issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"350 p. ; 21 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"In this phenomenal bestseller, Nobel Prize-winning physicist Richard P. Feynman recounts his adventures trading ideas on atomic physics with Einstein and Bohr and ideas on gambling with Nick the Greek, painting a naked female toreador, accompanying a ballet on his bongo drums--and much else of an eyebrow-raising and hilarious nature. Photos."},"tableOfContents":"From Far Rockaway to MIT. He fixes radios by thinking! ; String beans ; Who stole the door? ; Latin or Italian? ; Always trying to escape ; The Chief Research Chemist of the Metaplast Corporation -- The Princeton years. \"Surely you're joking, Mr. Feynman!\" ; Meeeeeeeeeee! ; A map of the cat? ; Monster minds ; Mixing paints ; A different box of tools ; Mindreaders ; The amateur scientist -- Feynman, the bomb, and the military. Fizzled fuses ; Testing bloodhounds ; Los Alamos from below ; Safecracker meets safecracker ; Uncle Sam doesn't need you! -- From Cornell to Caltech, with a touch of Brazil. The dignified professor ; Any questions? ; I want my dollar! ; You just ask them? ; Lucky numbers ; O Americano, outra vez! ; Man of a thousand tongues ; Certainly, Mr. Big! ; An offer you must refuse -- The world of one physicist. Would you solve the Dirac equation? ; The 7 percent solution ; Thirteen times ; It sounds Greek to me! ; But is it art? ; Is electricity fire? ; Judging books by their covers ; Alfred Nobel's other mistake ; Bringing culture to the physicists ; Found out in Paris ; Altered states ; Cargo cult science.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Richard P. Feynman as told to Ralph Leighton ; edited by Edward Hutchings."},"Includes index."],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Feynman, Richard Phillips"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Feynman, Richard P. (Richard Phillips)",{"@type":"date","#text":"1918-1988"}]}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Physicists","geographic":"United States","genre":"Biography"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Science","genre":"Humor"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"QC16.F49 A37 1997"},{"@authority":"nlm","#text":"B F435f"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0393316041 :"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"37123233"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990098355780203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000463633307","#text":"Lamont Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"QC16.F49 A37 1997x"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepositor